    "body": "Could we instead pass iommu as input to translate_gpa?  This would make the API stable for any future change and will match the prototype of other functions which take the iommu pointer as the first arguement. \r\n\r\n ```\r\nuint64_t\r\n translate_gpa (\r\n     iommu_t *iommu, iohgatp_t iohgatp, uint64_t gpa, uint64_t *spa) {\r\n```\r\n\r\nGXL can be obtained inside translate_gpa as follows:\r\n\r\n`if ( iohgatp.MODE == IOHGATP_Sv39x4 && iommu->reg_file.fctl.gxl == 0 ) {`\r\n\r\n\r\nThe callers then need to pass the iommu pointer:\r\n\r\n```\r\n-        if ( translate_gpa(iohgatp, a, &a) == -1) return -1;\r\n+        if ( translate_gpa(iommu, iohgatp, a, &a) == -1) return -1;\r\n\r\n```",
